1
00:00:37,971 --> 00:00:40,440
Yoo-hoo!

2
00:00:40,573 --> 00:00:44,177
Ah! This feels wonderful!

3
00:00:44,911 --> 00:00:47,080
The best hot spring in the country.

4
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,350
I'm so glad I came.

5
00:00:52,919 --> 00:00:53,753
Huh?

6
00:00:54,454 --> 00:00:55,388
Mixed bath?

7
00:00:56,089 --> 00:00:56,923
Men's bath.

8
00:00:57,257 --> 00:00:58,591
- Really?
- Really.

9
00:01:11,971 --> 00:01:14,374
Don't you just love riding local buses?

10
00:01:14,507 --> 00:01:15,608
You're too close.

11
00:01:16,276 --> 00:01:17,210
Sorry.

12
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:23,149
I drew a picture of you.

13
00:01:23,283 --> 00:01:25,118
This is you.

14
00:01:25,952 --> 00:01:27,854
- Me?
- Yes.

15
00:01:28,788 --> 00:01:30,190
It's a lousy drawing.

16
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,793
How much per month?

17
00:01:35,695 --> 00:01:37,664
I'll pay you to be my lover.

18
00:01:38,531 --> 00:01:39,499
I'll make you happy.

19
00:01:39,632 --> 00:01:40,800
Impossible.

20
00:01:46,072 --> 00:01:47,974
I said you're too close.

21
00:01:48,475 --> 00:01:50,143
Get away from me.

22
00:01:50,210 --> 00:01:51,044
Ow...

23
00:01:55,715 --> 00:01:56,683
Move.

24
00:02:01,921 --> 00:02:02,889
Are you okay?

25
00:02:04,457 --> 00:02:05,592
Are you okay?!

26
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:11,231
Ambulance!

27
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:35,288
Cardiopulmonary arrest.

28
00:02:35,421 --> 00:02:37,190
Help me lay him down.

29
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:38,358
Coming.

30
00:02:41,127 --> 00:02:42,028
Who are you?

31
00:02:43,429 --> 00:02:44,664
A surgeon passing by.

32
00:02:46,799 --> 00:02:48,134
We can't wait.

33
00:02:58,178 --> 00:02:59,012
Watch out!

34
00:02:59,078 --> 00:03:00,280
There's an emergency patient.

35
00:03:15,428 --> 00:03:17,297
Come on, breathe!

36
00:03:25,238 --> 00:03:26,272
He's coming back.

37
00:03:33,813 --> 00:03:36,683
There's a hospital below.
I got a van for you.

38
00:03:37,617 --> 00:03:38,518
It's you

39
00:03:39,018 --> 00:03:39,886
from minutes ago.

40
00:03:46,593 --> 00:03:47,493
What?

41
00:03:58,104 --> 00:03:59,205
Dr. Daimon?

42
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:03,309
Remember me? Morimoto from
Teito University Hospital 3.

43
00:04:03,409 --> 00:04:04,944
Possible cardiac tamponade.

44
00:04:05,111 --> 00:04:07,013
Where's the treatment room?

45
00:04:07,146 --> 00:04:08,248
Over there.

46
00:04:12,352 --> 00:04:14,921
Pericardial effusion.
He needs surgery.

47
00:04:15,588 --> 00:04:16,422
Surgery?

48
00:04:16,856 --> 00:04:19,525
I'm the only doctor and
there's no OR.

49
00:04:19,592 --> 00:04:20,526
We can't operate.

50
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,929
He'll die without surgery.

51
00:04:22,996 --> 00:04:24,063
We can do it here.

52
00:04:24,197 --> 00:04:27,533
If something happens,
I can't be responsible.

53
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:30,270
Subxiphoid approach.
Prepare local anesthesia.

54
00:04:30,336 --> 00:04:31,904
- Seriously?
- Hurry.

55
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:40,847
When did university hospitals
lose so much authority?

56
00:04:41,047 --> 00:04:44,417
Nobody ever used to
defy a professor.

57
00:04:45,485 --> 00:04:48,621
Young people get turned off
by stories of the past.

58
00:04:48,921 --> 00:04:53,359
We, the Japan Doctors Club,
have to change with the times.

59
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:07,006
I never thought
I'd be operating here.

60
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,508
Stop making a fuss.

61
00:05:09,642 --> 00:05:12,745
Your skills are still awesome.
I'm impressed.

62
00:05:14,881 --> 00:05:15,982
Have we met?

63
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:17,984
Pericardiotomy.

64
00:05:18,117 --> 00:05:19,285
Lift the xiphoid process.

65
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,054
Yes, Doctor.

66
00:05:38,404 --> 00:05:39,972
He needs another surgery ASAP.

67
00:05:40,039 --> 00:05:41,040
Another one?

68
00:05:41,107 --> 00:05:44,877
This was just emergency surgery,
not definitive.

69
00:05:53,152 --> 00:05:54,120
Nice job.

70
00:05:56,889 --> 00:05:59,659
Who is she?

71
00:06:01,828 --> 00:06:03,796
A freelance surgeon.

72
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,265
Freelance?

73
00:06:07,667 --> 00:06:08,634
Part-timer?

74
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:19,278
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

75
00:06:23,116 --> 00:06:25,651
SHIRETOKO

76
00:06:27,086 --> 00:06:28,821
A year in Shiretoko.

77
00:06:28,921 --> 00:06:33,659
Yesterday, a red fox was
playing in our yard.

78
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:35,661
It was right there the other day.

79
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:40,900
We had a staring contest. I lost.

80
00:06:41,167 --> 00:06:42,335
Honey!

81
00:06:42,568 --> 00:06:46,339
I'm bored to death here.

82
00:06:48,841 --> 00:06:49,675
Hanako...

83
00:06:50,543 --> 00:06:53,813
I'm not going back to Tokyo.

84
00:06:55,314 --> 00:06:57,450
The hospital's power struggle...

85
00:06:57,683 --> 00:07:00,086
I'm sick and tired of it.

86
00:07:00,486 --> 00:07:01,921
Pathetic.

87
00:07:03,756 --> 00:07:08,127
Without money and power,
you're worse than a cutlet.

88
00:07:08,494 --> 00:07:11,497
"Oh, how I miss the high life!"

89
00:07:11,831 --> 00:07:14,333
Worse than a cutlet?
What does that mean?

90
00:07:15,034 --> 00:07:16,135
Nothing.

91
00:07:20,339 --> 00:07:24,844
On the cape

92
00:07:25,077 --> 00:07:30,416
of Shiretoko...

93
00:07:30,883 --> 00:07:37,323
When rugosa roses bloom...

94
00:07:38,224 --> 00:07:44,397
Remember how it was...

95
00:07:45,264 --> 00:07:50,303
For you and me...

96
00:07:51,604 --> 00:07:52,438
Ebina?

97
00:07:52,572 --> 00:07:54,474
It's been so long,
Director Hiruma.

98
00:07:54,807 --> 00:07:55,675
Ma'am.

99
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:59,378
Have you been transferred here as well?

100
00:07:59,645 --> 00:08:01,814
Well, no...

101
00:08:01,881 --> 00:08:02,782
Ebina...

102
00:08:03,082 --> 00:08:06,586
You're back at Totei University Hospital?

103
00:08:06,919 --> 00:08:07,987
Yes.

104
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:09,789
- You're back?
- I am.

105
00:08:09,922 --> 00:08:13,493
And you're here because...

106
00:08:13,559 --> 00:08:14,427
I'm here...

107
00:08:16,229 --> 00:08:17,730
to take you back there.

108
00:08:17,897 --> 00:08:20,366
Wait. Hold on.

109
00:08:20,867 --> 00:08:21,901
So this means

110
00:08:22,835 --> 00:08:26,038
Totei University Main Hospital

111
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:28,074
wants me back?

112
00:08:28,875 --> 00:08:30,142
- They need me?
- Yes.

113
00:08:30,209 --> 00:08:32,044
They want me?

114
00:08:32,178 --> 00:08:33,846
- Yes sir.
- I missed hearing that.

115
00:08:33,913 --> 00:08:36,015
You bet I'll return.

116
00:08:36,949 --> 00:08:38,317
Former Director Hiruma.

117
00:08:38,918 --> 00:08:44,757
You needlessly purchased large
quantities of surgical equipment.

118
00:08:44,957 --> 00:08:49,829
You accepted huge bribes from
the vendors for your personal gain.

119
00:08:50,229 --> 00:08:52,331
Are these the facts?

120
00:08:54,133 --> 00:08:55,167
Ebina.

121
00:08:56,002 --> 00:08:57,169
Ebina.

122
00:08:58,104 --> 00:08:59,171
Did you set me up?

123
00:09:01,741 --> 00:09:02,909
Did you betray me?

124
00:09:04,176 --> 00:09:06,779
Please answer the question.

125
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:09,782
Former Director Hiruma.

126
00:09:11,651 --> 00:09:14,554
October 27, 2016.

127
00:09:15,721 --> 00:09:16,656
You...

128
00:09:18,291 --> 00:09:19,559
accepted this pouch

129
00:09:20,693 --> 00:09:23,396
containing a box of sweets
and $300,000.

130
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:28,167
We have a witness testimony.

131
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:33,406
There's no way $300,000
would fit in that small pouch.

132
00:09:33,472 --> 00:09:34,707
Is that what you think?

133
00:09:35,041 --> 00:09:36,309
- Hara.
- Yes!

134
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:46,819
You too, Takashi Hara?

135
00:09:47,687 --> 00:09:48,854
It's Mamoru.

136
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:51,757
Mamoru Hara. Sir!

137
00:09:54,126 --> 00:09:57,597
What a farce. This is ridiculous.

138
00:10:01,233 --> 00:10:04,637
I'm returning to the satellite
hospital in Shiretoko.

139
00:10:06,339 --> 00:10:08,708
Goodbye.

140
00:10:09,041 --> 00:10:10,309
One moment.

141
00:10:15,381 --> 00:10:19,552
I'm Shimura, the director
of Totei University Hospital.

142
00:10:22,655 --> 00:10:23,489
Dr. Hiruma.

143
00:10:23,589 --> 00:10:24,423
Yes?

144
00:10:24,991 --> 00:10:28,127
You have nowhere to return.

145
00:10:29,428 --> 00:10:33,332
You've been relieved of your duties
as the director of Shiretoko Hospital.

146
00:10:33,866 --> 00:10:34,700
What?

147
00:10:35,735 --> 00:10:38,270
Tell us exactly what happened.

148
00:10:41,507 --> 00:10:44,510
When I was the director
of Totei University Hospital

149
00:10:45,645 --> 00:10:47,446
everything I did was

150
00:10:48,581 --> 00:10:51,484
for the good of the hospital.

151
00:10:52,084 --> 00:10:53,519
Nothing out of self interest.

152
00:10:57,023 --> 00:10:58,224
Isn't that right, Ebina?

153
00:11:01,193 --> 00:11:02,895
Stop making excuses.

154
00:11:10,136 --> 00:11:13,239
To restore the hospital's
honor and integrity

155
00:11:14,573 --> 00:11:16,842
you must accept responsibility.

156
00:11:18,611 --> 00:11:19,578
Responsibility?

157
00:11:21,380 --> 00:11:22,682
What responsibility is that?

158
00:11:29,321 --> 00:11:30,756
<i>In 2017,</i>

159
00:11:31,390 --> 00:11:35,227
<i>the once sacrosanct</i>
<i>university medical system</i>

160
00:11:35,928 --> 00:11:37,530
<i>finally collapsed.</i>

161
00:11:39,765 --> 00:11:45,538
<i>Director Shimura will be</i>
<i>making her rounds now.</i>

162
00:11:48,441 --> 00:11:54,346
<i>University hospitals launched a reform</i>
<i>to regain their integrity.</i>

163
00:11:56,082 --> 00:11:58,918
<i>Eradicating the antiquated power structure</i>

164
00:11:59,285 --> 00:12:04,290
<i>to promote medical practices</i>
<i>that put the patients first.</i>

165
00:12:04,924 --> 00:12:07,359
I heard you went overseas to study

166
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:12,331
but didn't learn any new skills and
got shunted off to the boonies.

167
00:12:13,132 --> 00:12:15,367
- Director Shimura called me back.
- Why?

168
00:12:15,434 --> 00:12:16,869
Divine intervention.

169
00:12:16,936 --> 00:12:18,037
Divine intervention?

170
00:12:18,270 --> 00:12:19,872
Manifested by Dr. Daimon.

171
00:12:19,939 --> 00:12:22,608
Demon…I don't want to hear that name.

172
00:12:22,675 --> 00:12:24,276
Don't say it.

173
00:12:26,846 --> 00:12:31,717
<i>In the midst of reform, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

174
00:12:32,218 --> 00:12:36,689
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

175
00:12:38,124 --> 00:12:39,725
<i>This woman, for example</i>.

176
00:12:40,826 --> 00:12:44,830
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

177
00:12:45,898 --> 00:12:51,837
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

178
00:12:54,473 --> 00:12:57,042
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

179
00:12:57,543 --> 00:13:00,613
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

180
00:13:22,902 --> 00:13:29,108
Toxins that were crippling this hospital
have been completely purged.

181
00:13:29,842 --> 00:13:33,946
There is no longer a power structure
that puts the institution first.

182
00:13:35,414 --> 00:13:40,152
We must now achieve our integrity as
a university hospital.

183
00:13:40,252 --> 00:13:44,490
Teaching doctors,
clinical and basic research,

184
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:46,759
and high-quality medical care.

185
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:53,432
We must fulfill these three important
roles and put the patients first.

186
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:57,136
Let us be united in our efforts.

187
00:13:59,471 --> 00:14:01,273
Clean is beautiful.

188
00:14:01,473 --> 00:14:02,441
Stop it.

189
00:14:04,410 --> 00:14:05,878
- I'm sorry.
- He's hurt.

190
00:14:12,384 --> 00:14:13,219
Daimon!

191
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:15,688
Dr. Daimon!

192
00:14:16,622 --> 00:14:20,092
She's gorgeous.
One of you doctor's mistress?

193
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:22,261
- No.
- Absolutely not.

194
00:14:27,466 --> 00:14:28,701
You snatcher.

195
00:14:31,437 --> 00:14:32,805
Snatcher?

196
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:33,906
Wow...

197
00:14:33,973 --> 00:14:34,807
Yeah, wow.

198
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:36,242
Where's my patient?

199
00:14:39,712 --> 00:14:43,082
He needs another surgery ASAP.

200
00:14:44,583 --> 00:14:46,518
I've instructed that he should

201
00:14:47,486 --> 00:14:51,724
be operated here, a hospital with
the latest medical equipment.

202
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:57,029
I transferred him and also brought
his primary care physician.

203
00:14:57,496 --> 00:14:58,397
Primary care physician?

204
00:14:58,530 --> 00:15:00,032
Me, Dr. Daimon.

205
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:01,300
Me.

206
00:15:02,601 --> 00:15:04,136
You can't handle this op.

207
00:15:08,307 --> 00:15:11,310
- Daimon, long time no see.
- Scary face.

208
00:15:18,050 --> 00:15:20,753
It's been a while.
Good to see you.

209
00:15:20,819 --> 00:15:22,788
Do I know you?

210
00:15:23,856 --> 00:15:25,424
He's hurt.

211
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:30,129
You're extremely rude.

212
00:15:32,665 --> 00:15:33,899
Ignoring me?

213
00:15:35,367 --> 00:15:36,402
Get her out of here!

214
00:15:39,204 --> 00:15:40,139
Us?

215
00:15:40,906 --> 00:15:42,274
Forget it.

216
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:46,578
Hurry up, will you?

217
00:15:46,645 --> 00:15:47,980
- Wait.
- Ma'am?

218
00:15:51,216 --> 00:15:52,284
Ms. Daimon.

219
00:15:54,253 --> 00:15:57,256
We'll hire you at this hospital.

220
00:15:58,090 --> 00:15:59,391
Are you serious?

221
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,561
What is she doing?

222
00:16:02,661 --> 00:16:03,762
Director Shimura.

223
00:16:05,030 --> 00:16:07,333
- She's a freelancer.
- So?

224
00:16:12,404 --> 00:16:15,307
I watched her operate with my own eyes.

225
00:16:16,608 --> 00:16:18,711
It was a brilliant operation.

226
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:19,812
Thanks.

227
00:16:20,713 --> 00:16:23,983
A skilled surgeon doesn't require a title.

228
00:16:24,783 --> 00:16:26,285
Freelancer or whatever.

229
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:28,320
I accept you.

230
00:16:31,523 --> 00:16:35,227
Welcome, Dr. Michiko Daimon.

231
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:41,633
Welcome.

232
00:16:49,942 --> 00:16:51,477
Good job, Michiko.

233
00:16:51,543 --> 00:16:54,980
You got hired without my help.

234
00:16:55,114 --> 00:16:57,316
I have the contract.
It's signed.

235
00:16:59,551 --> 00:17:01,387
Riichi.

236
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,722
Already?
You're on a roll.

237
00:17:03,789 --> 00:17:04,723
Let me see.

238
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,860
- No.
- Not that. The contract.

239
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:09,294
Here.

240
00:17:11,897 --> 00:17:13,832
"Only $3,000?"

241
00:17:13,899 --> 00:17:16,535
She is Madam Clean after all.

242
00:17:16,602 --> 00:17:19,471
But that's too clean even for her.

243
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:20,806
Madam Clean?

244
00:17:21,006 --> 00:17:25,411
Madoka Shimura. After graduating
as the top student at med school,

245
00:17:26,178 --> 00:17:32,751
she climbed to the top of Totei Hospital
without personal connections.

246
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:37,990
She's nicknamed Madam Clean
because of her integrity.

247
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:42,961
Totei University Hospital is
capturing public attention.

248
00:17:43,695 --> 00:17:46,832
The hospital is implementing
an organizational reform

249
00:17:47,199 --> 00:17:51,370
that challenges its shady deals
with venders that were conceived

250
00:17:51,470 --> 00:17:53,939
under the hierarchical power
structure of the hospital.

251
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:58,010
The self-corrective actions
are spearheaded

252
00:17:58,110 --> 00:18:01,580
by its first-ever female director.

253
00:18:02,681 --> 00:18:08,620
Rumor has it that during her internship,
she was wooed by many professors

254
00:18:08,787 --> 00:18:12,091
who unsuccessfully tried to
make her their mistress.

255
00:18:12,257 --> 00:18:13,358
Is that right?

256
00:18:13,992 --> 00:18:14,927
Safe.

257
00:18:15,327 --> 00:18:19,398
Totei may actually change
as a medical institution.

258
00:18:19,465 --> 00:18:25,003
She won't allow her staff to neglect
the patients to play musical chairs.

259
00:18:25,137 --> 00:18:26,338
Safe.

260
00:18:27,873 --> 00:18:32,444
But they say fish don't grow
in rivers that are too clean.

261
00:18:32,578 --> 00:18:33,579
Oh yeah?

262
00:18:34,046 --> 00:18:39,585
The contract is too cheap.
I'll have to go re-negotiate.

263
00:18:39,718 --> 00:18:44,356
"Ron"! That's it!

264
00:18:44,456 --> 00:18:45,424
You're kidding.

265
00:18:45,491 --> 00:18:48,227
"Uradora" extra bonus...

266
00:18:50,028 --> 00:18:51,029
Only "riichi"?

267
00:18:51,130 --> 00:18:53,198
A cheap hand.

268
00:18:53,599 --> 00:18:55,234
You're too cheap.

269
00:18:55,334 --> 00:18:56,635
"Right, Ben Casey?"

270
00:18:56,702 --> 00:18:57,936
Cheap.

271
00:18:58,237 --> 00:18:59,872
Michiko Daimon.

272
00:19:00,472 --> 00:19:03,175
Special skills, surgery.
Hobby, surgery.

273
00:19:03,442 --> 00:19:06,512
The most difficult type
of doctor to work with.

274
00:19:09,448 --> 00:19:10,415
Excuse me.

275
00:19:12,217 --> 00:19:13,085
Yes?

276
00:19:13,152 --> 00:19:15,220
A word about Michiko Daimon.

277
00:19:16,388 --> 00:19:18,390
Why hire that dubious woman?

278
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:19,892
I told you.

279
00:19:21,193 --> 00:19:25,497
A skilled surgeon doesn't require a title.

280
00:19:26,798 --> 00:19:31,069
Where did you meet her in the first place?

281
00:19:34,573 --> 00:19:38,410
Where did I meet her?
Does it matter?

282
00:19:38,644 --> 00:19:42,514
You're attracting a great deal
of media attention.

283
00:19:44,449 --> 00:19:46,084
I'll keep that in mind.

284
00:19:47,052 --> 00:19:49,454
There's something else.

285
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:58,964
I heard that your birthday is
coming up next week.

286
00:19:59,464 --> 00:20:00,465
Happy birthday.

287
00:20:04,503 --> 00:20:06,905
Let us begin
the pre-op conference.

288
00:20:07,673 --> 00:20:10,309
The first case is
a 58-year-old male.

289
00:20:10,409 --> 00:20:11,643
Kazuhisa Kurumada.

290
00:20:11,877 --> 00:20:15,681
He was diagnosed with cardiac
infarction with coronary aneurysm

291
00:20:15,914 --> 00:20:17,950
complicated by cardiac tamponade.

292
00:20:19,051 --> 00:20:22,221
Mine! He's my patient.

293
00:20:22,354 --> 00:20:26,692
Dr. Daimon, a surgeon has
already been appointed for him.

294
00:20:26,925 --> 00:20:28,160
Yeah. Me.

295
00:20:28,293 --> 00:20:29,361
His surgeon is

296
00:20:30,229 --> 00:20:32,864
Prof. Jichael Mackson of
Harvard Medical School.

297
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:34,900
Prof. Jichael Mackson?!

298
00:20:35,601 --> 00:20:37,202
Who? Thriller?

299
00:20:56,021 --> 00:20:59,891
The world-famous cardiac surgeon
is coming here to operate?

300
00:21:00,025 --> 00:21:00,959
No.

301
00:21:01,226 --> 00:21:05,731
Prof. Mackson will remotely control
a surgical robot called Columbus

302
00:21:05,964 --> 00:21:09,701
via Internet from
his hospital in the US

303
00:21:09,968 --> 00:21:13,038
to operate on this patient in Japan.

304
00:21:14,806 --> 00:21:16,508
Robot? Remote control?

305
00:21:16,575 --> 00:21:21,813
We'll call it the
Trans-Pacific Telesurgery.

306
00:21:22,681 --> 00:21:25,417
Needless to say,
it's the first in medical history.

307
00:21:34,226 --> 00:21:38,730
This operation is a collaboration
between Japan and the US

308
00:21:39,064 --> 00:21:42,100
and a cutting-edge medical project.

309
00:21:42,234 --> 00:21:48,273
The latest medical care can be provided
to isolated communities with no doctors.

310
00:21:48,507 --> 00:21:54,613
I'm confident that it will be a beacon of
the "patients first" policy I advocate.

311
00:21:59,618 --> 00:22:01,286
Yes, Dr. Daimon?

312
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,089
He's my patient.
You don't get to decide.

313
00:22:04,389 --> 00:22:05,624
Daimon, watch yourself.

314
00:22:05,957 --> 00:22:10,929
Why? No need for that robot
when you have me.

315
00:22:14,466 --> 00:22:17,703
She thinks she can do
better than the robot?

316
00:22:17,869 --> 00:22:20,238
She has an outdated mindset.

317
00:22:20,305 --> 00:22:22,808
What a typical big mouth.

318
00:22:23,909 --> 00:22:26,611
Get this vixen out of here now!

319
00:22:31,049 --> 00:22:32,117
What?

320
00:22:33,251 --> 00:22:35,053
I'm going to lunch.

321
00:22:39,791 --> 00:22:40,926
She's a disgrace.

322
00:22:41,026 --> 00:22:42,027
Dr. Inomata.

323
00:22:42,594 --> 00:22:43,662
Yes?

324
00:22:45,997 --> 00:22:49,634
I can't take this.

325
00:22:51,169 --> 00:22:52,904
What is it? A rack?

326
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:57,709
Don't ever do this again.

327
00:23:00,011 --> 00:23:02,414
- Yes ma'am.
- No more "yes ma'am."

328
00:23:04,916 --> 00:23:09,855
I don't want to hear "yes ma'am"
or "yes sir" from any of you.

329
00:23:10,222 --> 00:23:11,490
Yes ma'am…Oops.

330
00:23:18,864 --> 00:23:20,399
"Yes sir" is forbidden.

331
00:23:21,633 --> 00:23:22,768
So what do we say?

332
00:23:25,003 --> 00:23:25,837
Noted.

333
00:23:30,342 --> 00:23:32,711
Master, the usual. With extra cabbage.

334
00:23:32,811 --> 00:23:35,680
And two servings of
rice and soup.

335
00:23:35,814 --> 00:23:38,116
You got it.

336
00:23:43,789 --> 00:23:44,856
Can I sit here?

337
00:23:44,923 --> 00:23:45,857
Go ahead.

338
00:23:49,327 --> 00:23:52,664
Hey, I've seen you before.

339
00:23:54,166 --> 00:23:55,233
Where was it?

340
00:23:56,802 --> 00:23:58,437
I'm busy here.

341
00:24:00,672 --> 00:24:03,942
I think you see him every day.

342
00:24:04,509 --> 00:24:09,381
He's Mr. Isshiki, a famous newscaster.

343
00:24:09,548 --> 00:24:12,017
Oh, the guy on TV.

344
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:14,853
Here you go. The special cutlet.

345
00:24:25,397 --> 00:24:26,798
It's yours.

346
00:24:27,466 --> 00:24:28,967
Go ahead and eat it.

347
00:24:29,568 --> 00:24:33,371
But this is the special cutlet.
I ordered the regular.

348
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:34,506
It's okay.

349
00:24:34,606 --> 00:24:35,474
Really?

350
00:24:38,210 --> 00:24:39,177
Thanks.

351
00:24:46,551 --> 00:24:49,221
Special cutlet! Yum!

352
00:25:04,703 --> 00:25:05,670
What's wrong?

353
00:25:09,641 --> 00:25:10,909
Jugular vein distention.

354
00:25:11,877 --> 00:25:13,512
Call an ambulance.

355
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:20,619
It couldn't have grown
this big unnoticed.

356
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:24,723
A 7-cm tumor in the right
ventricle of your heart.

357
00:25:26,725 --> 00:25:29,928
You must have known about your condition.

358
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:34,966
Yes.

359
00:25:35,600 --> 00:25:37,002
You'll die without surgery.

360
00:25:38,236 --> 00:25:39,804
Blunt, aren't you?

361
00:25:41,306 --> 00:25:43,074
It's not too late yet.

362
00:25:44,809 --> 00:25:45,644
Not too late?

363
00:25:45,777 --> 00:25:47,679
I can cut out the whole tumor.

364
00:25:50,448 --> 00:25:51,816
No need to console me.

365
00:25:52,717 --> 00:25:53,718
Console you?

366
00:25:56,521 --> 00:25:58,957
I won't survive
one way or the other.

367
00:25:59,391 --> 00:26:05,730
Every doctor I've seen said
it can't be completely removed.

368
00:26:11,536 --> 00:26:13,738
Rather than convalescing
after an operation

369
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:18,743
I want to keep working
until I drop dead.

370
00:26:20,545 --> 00:26:23,982
I know how to live my life.

371
00:26:29,187 --> 00:26:31,056
You're acting tough but...

372
00:26:33,658 --> 00:26:34,926
You've given up.

373
00:26:43,768 --> 00:26:45,904
This patient is in our hospital?

374
00:26:46,004 --> 00:26:48,006
Yes ma'am. I said it again.

375
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:52,077
Yes. Daimon admitted him.

376
00:26:52,544 --> 00:26:54,713
And unfortunately, he's...

377
00:26:56,014 --> 00:26:59,250
- Journalist Tatsuo Isshiki.
- Yes.

378
00:26:59,317 --> 00:27:02,020
That part-timer should've
minded her own business.

379
00:27:02,120 --> 00:27:04,623
We can't let a celebrity
like him die here.

380
00:27:04,723 --> 00:27:06,725
We should release him right away.

381
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:09,995
You're right.

382
00:27:10,695 --> 00:27:11,730
Excuse me.

383
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:13,498
Daimon.

384
00:27:19,938 --> 00:27:21,506
Let me cut this patient.

385
00:27:21,806 --> 00:27:24,142
His tumor can't be completely removed.

386
00:27:24,876 --> 00:27:26,811
Can't you even see that?

387
00:27:27,012 --> 00:27:29,047
No. Because it can be.

388
00:27:30,015 --> 00:27:31,049
What?

389
00:27:31,116 --> 00:27:34,019
Separate the tumor from
normal cardiac muscle.

390
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:36,554
Complete resection with a 5-mm margin.

391
00:27:36,621 --> 00:27:37,656
Surgery is possible.

392
00:27:38,056 --> 00:27:41,960
What if you have to remove
the interventricular septum?

393
00:27:42,027 --> 00:27:43,862
I'll use the double-patch closure.

394
00:27:49,100 --> 00:27:51,603
Absurd. A pipe dream.

395
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:54,472
Nobody's skilled enough to do that.

396
00:27:54,606 --> 00:27:55,774
I am.

397
00:27:57,475 --> 00:27:59,577
Don't be so cocky, part-timer!

398
00:28:00,011 --> 00:28:03,114
This is the great Totei
University Hospital. Get out!

399
00:28:03,381 --> 00:28:04,482
Fine.

400
00:28:06,117 --> 00:28:08,319
- Let's do it.
- Yes, let's…What?

401
00:28:08,386 --> 00:28:09,554
I'll run the tests.

402
00:28:09,621 --> 00:28:11,923
I'll ask Prof. Mackson to operate on him.

403
00:28:12,824 --> 00:28:16,161
You can't be serious.
I'm the only one good enough.

404
00:28:17,829 --> 00:28:19,464
Don't be so presumptuous.

405
00:28:22,300 --> 00:28:26,471
Only the best surgeon assisted by Columbus

406
00:28:27,138 --> 00:28:30,709
the state-of-the-art surgical robot

407
00:28:30,809 --> 00:28:34,179
will be able to completely
resect the tumor.

408
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:37,515
The surgery must not fail.

409
00:28:37,582 --> 00:28:39,451
- I never fail.
- Dr. Daimon.

410
00:28:40,618 --> 00:28:45,023
I'd like you to operate on Mr. Kurumada.

411
00:28:46,091 --> 00:28:48,326
He's originally your patient.

412
00:28:54,432 --> 00:28:59,270
And so, Dr. Daimon here
will be your surgeon.

413
00:28:59,637 --> 00:29:00,872
I see.

414
00:29:01,973 --> 00:29:06,177
But she's a part-timer, right?

415
00:29:06,611 --> 00:29:12,817
I hear the famous American surgeon
is operating on a celebrity.

416
00:29:12,917 --> 00:29:18,890
I guess a poor man like me can
be tossed over to a part-timer.

417
00:29:19,124 --> 00:29:21,025
That's not how it is.

418
00:29:21,860 --> 00:29:26,364
Whatever. I know how things
work at university hospitals.

419
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:31,136
Hospital reform. Patients first.

420
00:29:31,736 --> 00:29:34,405
It's all a bunch of crap.

421
00:29:35,373 --> 00:29:37,308
You're actually in luck.

422
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:40,779
I'm good at surgeries.

423
00:29:45,049 --> 00:29:45,984
I'm sorry.

424
00:29:48,153 --> 00:29:49,154
Sorry.

425
00:29:49,921 --> 00:29:53,224
The minutes from
the rogatory commission.

426
00:29:53,491 --> 00:29:56,060
You're supported by the public.

427
00:29:57,829 --> 00:29:59,964
The media loves you.

428
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:01,499
I appreciate that.

429
00:30:01,599 --> 00:30:04,102
Let's not talk business tonight.

430
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:06,471
Why don't you eat?

431
00:30:07,205 --> 00:30:08,106
No, thank you.

432
00:30:08,173 --> 00:30:11,075
The steaks here are delicious.

433
00:30:11,409 --> 00:30:12,544
The other day

434
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:18,516
Totei University Hospital received
the bill from your previous gathering.

435
00:30:21,085 --> 00:30:22,787
Tonight's meal...

436
00:30:23,655 --> 00:30:26,891
Who's paying for it under what pretext?

437
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:32,230
This club comprising executives
of university hospitals

438
00:30:32,297 --> 00:30:35,066
controls every hospital in the country.

439
00:30:36,401 --> 00:30:38,570
It has to end or else

440
00:30:39,270 --> 00:30:44,843
a clean and true "patients first"
policy will never be upheld.

441
00:30:46,144 --> 00:30:47,111
You're right.

442
00:30:48,313 --> 00:30:49,914
I must excuse myself now.

443
00:30:52,750 --> 00:30:55,820
You all enjoy your dinner.

444
00:31:00,592 --> 00:31:04,095
She makes a good steak taste bad.

445
00:31:04,729 --> 00:31:06,197
My appetite is ruined.

446
00:31:08,566 --> 00:31:12,503
Yes, the steak is delicious.
You should enjoy it.

447
00:31:13,304 --> 00:31:14,239
Dr. Hiruma.

448
00:31:14,339 --> 00:31:16,207
It's been a while.

449
00:31:16,407 --> 00:31:18,509
If you will allow me

450
00:31:19,143 --> 00:31:24,215
I will cover all the costs
for tonight's gathering.

451
00:31:26,851 --> 00:31:27,852
May I?

452
00:31:27,952 --> 00:31:28,953
Please.

453
00:31:29,087 --> 00:31:30,121
Thank you.

454
00:31:30,255 --> 00:31:31,389
Thank you indeed.

455
00:31:32,156 --> 00:31:36,461
Good evening, gentlemen.
It's nice to see you all.

456
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:38,096
- Dr. Hiruma.
- Yes?

457
00:31:38,429 --> 00:31:40,965
We're longing for good steak.

458
00:31:41,299 --> 00:31:42,767
I'm sure you are, Mr. Chairman.

459
00:31:43,534 --> 00:31:45,904
I can read between the lines.

460
00:31:46,170 --> 00:31:47,338
Between the lines?

461
00:31:47,472 --> 00:31:48,840
Yes, between the lines.

462
00:31:54,612 --> 00:31:56,915
It's incredible nowadays.

463
00:31:57,081 --> 00:31:59,550
Operating from the other
side of the Pacific.

464
00:31:59,717 --> 00:32:02,720
Maybe one day, you can be on Earth and

465
00:32:02,820 --> 00:32:05,290
operate on patients in a space station.

466
00:32:05,356 --> 00:32:09,260
If it's a space station,
I want to go there and operate.

467
00:32:09,394 --> 00:32:12,997
Treating the patient in front of you
could be a thing of the past.

468
00:32:13,298 --> 00:32:14,399
You think so?

469
00:32:14,699 --> 00:32:20,204
The important thing is to see and
feel the patient who's right there.

470
00:32:20,538 --> 00:32:23,141
You don't see at all.

471
00:32:23,274 --> 00:32:25,710
The meat in front
of you is burnt.

472
00:32:28,579 --> 00:32:30,148
You took all the good ones.

473
00:32:39,524 --> 00:32:42,794
MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL

474
00:33:03,915 --> 00:33:05,149
What is this?

475
00:33:05,350 --> 00:33:06,617
Such a small team.

476
00:33:07,218 --> 00:33:08,553
Everyone's over there.

477
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:12,190
- Over there?
- Prof. Mackson's telesurgery.

478
00:33:13,624 --> 00:33:16,294
But they all just watch him operate.

479
00:33:16,594 --> 00:33:17,895
They don't have to be there.

480
00:33:17,962 --> 00:33:19,063
I know but...

481
00:33:21,866 --> 00:33:22,967
Dr. Jonouchi too?

482
00:33:23,101 --> 00:33:25,670
She's probably there for the money.

483
00:33:26,537 --> 00:33:28,039
I should have known.

484
00:33:28,373 --> 00:33:32,343
Vitals. BP 105 over 68.
Heart rate 65.

485
00:33:32,877 --> 00:33:34,612
Starting extracorporeal circulation.

486
00:34:06,744 --> 00:34:08,179
Amazing.

487
00:34:22,393 --> 00:34:25,163
The ascending aorta is
attached to the sternum.

488
00:34:25,630 --> 00:34:27,065
It's attached rigidly.

489
00:34:27,498 --> 00:34:29,467
Starting detachment.
Grip the blood vessel.

490
00:34:29,534 --> 00:34:30,368
Okay.

491
00:34:30,435 --> 00:34:31,669
DeBakey.

492
00:34:36,841 --> 00:34:38,409
Sorry. I'll stop the bleeding.

493
00:34:38,509 --> 00:34:39,544
Short Satinsky.

494
00:34:42,547 --> 00:34:43,514
Don't get sloppy.

495
00:34:43,648 --> 00:34:44,582
Sorry.

496
00:34:47,919 --> 00:34:50,221
What are you doing?
Take the suction tip.

497
00:34:50,321 --> 00:34:51,589
Long Satinsky.

498
00:34:52,890 --> 00:34:54,725
Change ECC to femoral artery.

499
00:34:54,992 --> 00:34:55,827
Get ready.

500
00:34:56,394 --> 00:34:57,261
I need more hands.

501
00:34:57,328 --> 00:34:59,097
Get people from the other OR.

502
00:34:59,230 --> 00:35:01,299
I'll proceed. Metzen.

503
00:35:15,713 --> 00:35:17,248
This is fascinating.

504
00:35:17,715 --> 00:35:19,517
I'm simply awestruck.

505
00:35:19,617 --> 00:35:21,486
Bravo. Bravo.

506
00:35:25,123 --> 00:35:29,026
There's an emergency.
We need assistance in OR 2.

507
00:35:29,560 --> 00:35:30,895
Did Daimon fail?

508
00:35:31,395 --> 00:35:35,199
I don't believe it.
Part-timers shouldn't be trusted.

509
00:35:39,337 --> 00:35:42,640
Drs. Hara, Nishiyama, Ito. Go to OR 2.

510
00:35:44,175 --> 00:35:45,510
To assist a part-timer.

511
00:35:45,710 --> 00:35:47,145
- Dr. Hara.
- All right.

512
00:35:47,845 --> 00:35:48,746
I'll assist her.

513
00:35:49,213 --> 00:35:50,081
Let's go.

514
00:35:50,748 --> 00:35:52,416
Come on. Let's go.

515
00:35:52,517 --> 00:35:53,384
I want to stay.

516
00:35:53,451 --> 00:35:56,220
Drop it. We have to go.

517
00:35:56,787 --> 00:35:58,256
But Dr. Daimon...

518
00:35:58,489 --> 00:35:59,357
Damn.

519
00:36:00,458 --> 00:36:01,425
BP isn't increasing.

520
00:36:03,528 --> 00:36:04,462
Continuing the pump.

521
00:36:07,665 --> 00:36:08,699
Dr. Daimon.

522
00:36:08,766 --> 00:36:10,201
It was my fault.

523
00:36:11,202 --> 00:36:12,870
Start ECC.

524
00:36:16,541 --> 00:36:18,743
Clamp the aortic arch. Satinsky.

525
00:36:19,210 --> 00:36:20,144
Suction.

526
00:36:20,411 --> 00:36:21,479
Retractor.

527
00:36:22,380 --> 00:36:23,347
Repairing damage.

528
00:36:23,414 --> 00:36:24,949
5-0 nylon.

529
00:36:36,894 --> 00:36:37,762
Oh no.

530
00:36:39,096 --> 00:36:40,731
Start suction.

531
00:36:46,737 --> 00:36:48,506
- Suction?
- I'm on it.

532
00:37:00,318 --> 00:37:01,285
QT ANALYSIS FAILURE

533
00:37:01,419 --> 00:37:03,454
Blood conservation level dropping.

534
00:37:03,654 --> 00:37:07,325
Perfusion pressure, down in 50s.
Administering RBC.

535
00:37:08,593 --> 00:37:09,493
Not good.

536
00:37:10,294 --> 00:37:11,562
I can't see.

537
00:37:12,663 --> 00:37:13,798
Remove the robot.

538
00:37:13,864 --> 00:37:16,167
- Switch to thoracotomy.
- Thoracotomy?

539
00:37:16,300 --> 00:37:17,802
Change the procedure?

540
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:18,903
Hurry up!

541
00:37:19,070 --> 00:37:20,137
Removing robot.

542
00:37:20,338 --> 00:37:22,707
Do it! Hurry, Arima!

543
00:37:28,346 --> 00:37:30,214
It doesn't look good.

544
00:37:35,886 --> 00:37:37,655
Who's taking over?

545
00:37:37,888 --> 00:37:40,558
Not me. Dr. Ebina?

546
00:37:40,658 --> 00:37:43,894
I can't do it either. Dr. Torii?

547
00:37:44,428 --> 00:37:46,330
I have a dissertation to write.

548
00:37:46,697 --> 00:37:49,200
Dissertation? Now?

549
00:37:49,600 --> 00:37:51,235
Dr. Torii!

550
00:37:51,302 --> 00:37:53,537
Who's going to operate?!

551
00:38:02,280 --> 00:38:03,281
Director.

552
00:38:05,416 --> 00:38:06,717
How's the circulation?

553
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:10,855
Administering RBC.
Perfusion pressure back up in 60s.

554
00:38:13,024 --> 00:38:19,997
Starting reparation of damaged blood
vessel and resection of cardiac tumor.

555
00:38:20,531 --> 00:38:21,866
Scalpel.

556
00:38:30,007 --> 00:38:31,409
Monopolar.

557
00:38:32,810 --> 00:38:33,844
Tweezers.

558
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:57,201
Damage repaired.

559
00:38:57,735 --> 00:38:58,569
Thank God.

560
00:38:58,936 --> 00:39:02,807
Now detaching the internal thoracic artery
and bypass to the LAD.

561
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:03,941
Ultrasonic scalpel.

562
00:39:13,417 --> 00:39:15,453
Unbelievable.

563
00:39:17,922 --> 00:39:18,989
So fast.

564
00:39:29,767 --> 00:39:31,235
Blood vessel repaired.

565
00:39:32,370 --> 00:39:33,237
Raise the loupes.

566
00:39:33,304 --> 00:39:36,407
PP up in 70s.
Circulation is also stable.

567
00:39:43,080 --> 00:39:44,648
Incision into the right ventricle.

568
00:39:45,082 --> 00:39:46,450
11 blade.

569
00:39:51,956 --> 00:39:53,057
Brilliant.

570
00:39:56,694 --> 00:39:57,528
Brava.

571
00:39:57,828 --> 00:39:59,797
Right ventricular wall incised.

572
00:40:05,970 --> 00:40:09,106
Tumor invasion is more extensive
than we thought.

573
00:40:10,074 --> 00:40:12,143
And indistinct boundary
with normal tissue.

574
00:40:13,878 --> 00:40:16,614
Complete removal isn't possible.

575
00:40:17,581 --> 00:40:20,785
We should stop now and
switch to medical treatment.

576
00:40:24,054 --> 00:40:24,889
Monopolar.

577
00:40:26,590 --> 00:40:28,125
It's too dangerous to proceed.

578
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:31,028
Continuing the procedure
isn't putting the patient first.

579
00:40:31,095 --> 00:40:32,029
Director.

580
00:40:33,330 --> 00:40:34,298
Director!

581
00:40:56,187 --> 00:40:57,121
Inoperable.

582
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:00,724
Keep him open.

583
00:41:00,925 --> 00:41:02,026
Dr. Daimon...

584
00:41:02,092 --> 00:41:03,127
What are you doing?

585
00:41:03,294 --> 00:41:04,895
I'll get it out.

586
00:41:05,663 --> 00:41:07,164
Or he won't be cured.

587
00:41:07,264 --> 00:41:09,366
Don't be stupid. This is crazy.

588
00:41:09,900 --> 00:41:11,702
This is too difficult for a part-timer.

589
00:41:12,169 --> 00:41:15,606
You could kill him. What if you fail?

590
00:41:16,507 --> 00:41:18,309
I never fail.

591
00:41:22,813 --> 00:41:23,647
Pump?

592
00:41:23,714 --> 00:41:27,585
Therapeutic hypothermia at 28 degrees.
PP stable at 75.

593
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:30,821
Composite resection of
tumor and normal issue.

594
00:41:30,888 --> 00:41:31,889
Assist me.

595
00:41:53,911 --> 00:41:55,246
The incredible Demon.

596
00:41:56,580 --> 00:41:57,781
Impressive as always.

597
00:42:14,932 --> 00:42:18,669
Tumor removed.
Get the resection margin tested.

598
00:42:19,336 --> 00:42:21,205
Bovine pericardium for right ventricle.

599
00:42:21,272 --> 00:42:24,708
Cryoablation of tissue boundary.
Prepare the cryoprobe.

600
00:42:26,143 --> 00:42:27,745
Patching the ventricular septum.

601
00:42:27,811 --> 00:42:29,246
- Loupes.
- Here you go.

602
00:42:31,815 --> 00:42:33,551
Freeze the myocardium?

603
00:42:34,485 --> 00:42:35,519
I see.

604
00:42:36,020 --> 00:42:38,856
Freeze and kill the heart tissue

605
00:42:38,956 --> 00:42:42,560
to prevent arrhythmia and
destroy invisible cancer cells.

606
00:42:54,838 --> 00:42:56,073
Finished. Vitals?

607
00:42:56,206 --> 00:42:59,843
BP 115 over 84.
Pulse 78, normal sinus rhythm.

608
00:43:10,020 --> 00:43:11,055
Thank you, Doctor.

609
00:43:11,155 --> 00:43:12,122
Good job.

610
00:43:13,123 --> 00:43:13,958
Dr. Daimon.

611
00:43:21,332 --> 00:43:22,499
Thank you.

612
00:43:46,357 --> 00:43:50,227
Mr. Isshiki, the journalist, suffers
no post-op complications.

613
00:43:50,394 --> 00:43:52,096
Test results are also good.

614
00:43:52,596 --> 00:43:57,635
All thanks to the wonderful
surgery you performed.

615
00:43:58,068 --> 00:43:59,003
Brava!

616
00:44:01,271 --> 00:44:02,573
Excuse me.

617
00:44:03,674 --> 00:44:07,578
I'm Kanbara from
the Kanbara Locum Doctor Agency.

618
00:44:08,012 --> 00:44:10,280
Director Shimura, thank you

619
00:44:10,547 --> 00:44:15,452
for employing Michiko Daimon and
Hiromi Jonouchi from our agency.

620
00:44:15,986 --> 00:44:16,987
Melon.

621
00:44:19,890 --> 00:44:21,325
The bill.

622
00:44:23,994 --> 00:44:25,696
I can't accept the melon.

623
00:44:26,497 --> 00:44:28,165
It's of the highest quality.

624
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:30,134
Please take it back.

625
00:44:30,367 --> 00:44:31,402
For you then.

626
00:44:31,502 --> 00:44:34,071
Is that right? How nice.

627
00:44:36,940 --> 00:44:37,875
I'm sorry.

628
00:44:44,948 --> 00:44:45,916
I see.

629
00:44:47,418 --> 00:44:50,688
I've never seen such an exorbitant fee.

630
00:44:52,156 --> 00:44:55,025
Re-issue it with an appropriate amount.

631
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:57,294
May I?

632
00:45:00,130 --> 00:45:01,565
"$200,000"

633
00:45:01,632 --> 00:45:03,834
$200,000? This is insane.

634
00:45:04,435 --> 00:45:06,537
And where is this melon from?

635
00:45:08,672 --> 00:45:13,377
Daimon perfectly fixed the problem
caused by the surgery robot

636
00:45:13,844 --> 00:45:17,481
and rescued the hospital
from a dire crisis.

637
00:45:17,848 --> 00:45:22,686
Rest assured. I don't plan on
revealing the incidents in the OR.

638
00:45:23,020 --> 00:45:27,357
Daimon and Jonouchi will
also take it to their graves.

639
00:45:27,758 --> 00:45:28,826
Furthermore

640
00:45:28,926 --> 00:45:34,865
Daimon also successfully
performed the other surgery.

641
00:45:35,365 --> 00:45:41,338
Considering all that, I believe
the amount is quite reasonable.

642
00:45:45,109 --> 00:45:47,044
I heard that.

643
00:45:47,945 --> 00:45:50,581
Reasonable? Really?

644
00:45:50,981 --> 00:45:53,417
Your fees are usually unscrupulous.

645
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:57,921
Look who's here.
Former Director Hiruma.

646
00:45:58,021 --> 00:46:01,658
Shall I pay the fee on your behalf?

647
00:46:03,260 --> 00:46:05,929
You can't be serious, Dr. Hiruma.

648
00:46:08,031 --> 00:46:11,068
You don't belong here anymore.

649
00:46:11,535 --> 00:46:14,404
No, I don't. But...

650
00:46:15,372 --> 00:46:19,543
I'm worried about something.

651
00:46:20,077 --> 00:46:23,313
So I swallowed my pride and dropped in.

652
00:46:24,581 --> 00:46:26,250
- Ebina.
- Yes?

653
00:46:26,550 --> 00:46:31,155
A galley proof for a magazine
to be issued this week.

654
00:46:31,555 --> 00:46:33,357
Show it to Director Shimura.

655
00:46:37,928 --> 00:46:40,063
SHIMURA IN EXTRAMARITAL AFFAIR

656
00:46:40,197 --> 00:46:42,266
WITH JOURNALIST TATSUO ISSHIKI

657
00:46:42,533 --> 00:46:43,500
Mistress?

658
00:46:43,967 --> 00:46:45,469
It's our patient, Mr. Isshiki.

659
00:46:45,869 --> 00:46:47,070
That's his room here.

660
00:46:47,604 --> 00:46:49,506
Sucking lips in the hospital.

661
00:47:00,350 --> 00:47:02,452
This is a frightening situation.

662
00:47:03,720 --> 00:47:06,023
Director Madoka Shimura...

663
00:47:08,091 --> 00:47:10,327
Your "patients first" policy.

664
00:47:11,094 --> 00:47:14,331
You used it as a cover
to save your lover's life.

665
00:47:16,466 --> 00:47:19,203
You abused your authority
as the director

666
00:47:20,103 --> 00:47:22,039
and exploited the hospital.

667
00:47:23,440 --> 00:47:28,879
This is more like "lovers first"
rather than "patients first."

668
00:47:29,880 --> 00:47:31,248
Highly unethical.

669
00:47:35,085 --> 00:47:37,321
Indeed a frightening situation.

670
00:47:37,921 --> 00:47:38,889
Isn't it?

671
00:47:39,189 --> 00:47:40,858
Director Shimura!

672
00:47:40,991 --> 00:47:42,759
Director Shimura!

673
00:47:42,893 --> 00:47:45,362
Is it true about the affair?

674
00:47:55,606 --> 00:47:58,876
Knock on wood!
Knock on wood!

675
00:48:01,912 --> 00:48:04,014
SURGERY DEPARTMENT OFFICE

676
00:48:04,147 --> 00:48:07,084
Dr. Hara! Did you hear?!

677
00:48:08,852 --> 00:48:10,687
ADULTERY

678
00:48:10,754 --> 00:48:12,122
Is this for real?

679
00:48:12,256 --> 00:48:13,090
Yeah.

680
00:48:13,290 --> 00:48:16,326
The director's clean image
is ripped to shreds.

681
00:48:16,660 --> 00:48:17,895
As well as this hospital.

682
00:48:18,061 --> 00:48:19,863
Are things going to change again?

683
00:48:19,930 --> 00:48:21,131
Kissing the patient.

684
00:48:22,366 --> 00:48:24,134
She's pretty bold.

685
00:48:32,776 --> 00:48:33,644
Hello.

686
00:48:37,114 --> 00:48:38,749
You eat cutlets, huh?

687
00:48:39,249 --> 00:48:40,417
He likes them.

688
00:48:41,652 --> 00:48:43,053
We used to eat here often.

689
00:48:45,289 --> 00:48:46,723
I knew about your relationship.

690
00:48:50,527 --> 00:48:52,596
He was sitting next to you.

691
00:48:53,297 --> 00:48:54,264
Watch out!

692
00:48:54,331 --> 00:48:55,799
There's an emergency patient.

693
00:48:59,870 --> 00:49:01,738
A trip together to the hot spring.

694
00:49:07,344 --> 00:49:09,313
What a mishap.

695
00:49:11,014 --> 00:49:14,284
You brought him to the hospital.

696
00:49:15,385 --> 00:49:19,723
If you hadn't, we could have kept
our relationship under wraps.

697
00:49:21,458 --> 00:49:23,560
I would still be the director.

698
00:49:27,931 --> 00:49:28,966
So what?

699
00:49:30,133 --> 00:49:33,403
Your affair was exposed.
You lost your position.

700
00:49:33,737 --> 00:49:35,372
But you saved a life.

701
00:49:36,440 --> 00:49:38,075
You didn't fail.

702
00:49:43,580 --> 00:49:44,548
You're right.

703
00:49:47,351 --> 00:49:51,021
But something's puzzling me.

704
00:49:51,955 --> 00:49:56,259
Why did he agree to surgery
when he was so against it?

705
00:49:58,295 --> 00:49:59,329
Dr. Daimon.

706
00:50:00,197 --> 00:50:02,232
How did you convince him?

707
00:50:03,700 --> 00:50:06,103
I didn't convince him of anything.

708
00:50:08,038 --> 00:50:09,806
I can definitely cure you.

709
00:50:11,608 --> 00:50:13,043
I never fail.

710
00:50:22,085 --> 00:50:23,253
I see.

711
00:50:25,489 --> 00:50:27,858
I couldn't have said...

712
00:50:29,292 --> 00:50:30,994
"I never fail."

713
00:50:35,766 --> 00:50:37,501
All right.

714
00:50:47,811 --> 00:50:48,879
Hello.

715
00:50:51,248 --> 00:50:53,383
I'm Isshiki's wife.

716
00:50:57,120 --> 00:50:58,555
Snatcher!

717
00:51:10,267 --> 00:51:11,201
Take care.

718
00:51:14,571 --> 00:51:15,672
Scary.

719
00:51:17,908 --> 00:51:23,180
I apologize for the scandal
my private life has caused.

720
00:51:24,848 --> 00:51:31,354
As reported, Former Director Shimura
of Totei University Hospital and I were

721
00:51:32,522 --> 00:51:34,458
in an inappropriate relationship.

722
00:51:35,492 --> 00:51:36,526
However

723
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:41,498
she saved my life.

724
00:51:43,500 --> 00:51:45,368
I am truly grateful to her.

725
00:51:46,036 --> 00:51:48,171
What is he talking about?

726
00:51:48,338 --> 00:51:50,874
It was Michiko who saved his life.

727
00:51:51,341 --> 00:51:54,010
This is why I don't trust TV.

728
00:51:54,244 --> 00:51:55,946
Right, Ben Casey?

729
00:51:59,950 --> 00:52:01,985
Michiko, let's go.

730
00:52:03,353 --> 00:52:04,454
Michiko!

731
00:52:07,224 --> 00:52:10,260
My dear staff at
Totei University Hospital.

732
00:52:11,261 --> 00:52:12,129
Good morning.

733
00:52:13,497 --> 00:52:14,998
Good morning.

734
00:52:15,999 --> 00:52:19,903
I am convinced that the authority of
Totei University Hospital is

735
00:52:20,770 --> 00:52:21,738
the one and only

736
00:52:22,472 --> 00:52:26,209
driving force for the progress
of medicine in Japan.

737
00:52:27,344 --> 00:52:30,413
I have returned

738
00:52:31,014 --> 00:52:33,116
as its director.

739
00:52:34,484 --> 00:52:35,485
I'm back.

740
00:52:35,752 --> 00:52:37,521
- Welcome back!
- Welcome back!

741
00:52:39,089 --> 00:52:40,023
Welcome back.

742
00:52:41,858 --> 00:52:45,295
I hope you'll work together
under my direction

743
00:52:46,363 --> 00:52:49,232
to reclaim the authority

744
00:52:50,167 --> 00:52:53,003
of Totei University Hospital.

745
00:52:53,403 --> 00:52:54,337
Yes sir.

746
00:52:55,639 --> 00:52:57,574
I love the sound of that.

747
00:52:57,874 --> 00:52:59,176
Music to my ears.

748
00:52:59,476 --> 00:53:00,610
Yes sir…

749
00:53:00,677 --> 00:53:06,183
Now let us sing loud and proud.

750
00:53:07,150 --> 00:53:09,052
"The One and Only."

751
00:53:09,286 --> 00:53:10,420
Yes sir.

752
00:53:10,687 --> 00:53:14,291
The one and only

753
00:53:14,357 --> 00:53:18,461
No other mountain as high as us

754
00:53:18,562 --> 00:53:22,933
The breeze follows and covers us

755
00:53:22,999 --> 00:53:24,100
What's going on?

756
00:53:24,434 --> 00:53:25,635
Shall we join them?

757
00:53:26,570 --> 00:53:31,041
Totei! Totei! Totei! Totei!

758
00:53:31,775 --> 00:53:32,609
Daimon!

759
00:53:33,043 --> 00:53:34,077
What are you doing?

760
00:53:34,744 --> 00:53:39,649
And it's the one and only

761
00:53:41,651 --> 00:53:44,087
Succeeding Director Hiruma.

762
00:53:44,354 --> 00:53:47,757
Thank you for signing a contract

763
00:53:47,958 --> 00:53:49,326
with our Michiko Daimon.

764
00:53:49,426 --> 00:53:50,260
Contract?

765
00:53:50,393 --> 00:53:52,596
What's going on, Director Hiruma?

766
00:53:53,096 --> 00:53:55,665
I hired her.

767
00:53:55,799 --> 00:53:56,766
You hired her?

768
00:54:00,570 --> 00:54:05,308
There are conditions we'd like
you to observe without fail.

769
00:54:07,143 --> 00:54:07,978
There you go.

770
00:54:09,279 --> 00:54:10,380
There you go.

771
00:54:12,682 --> 00:54:13,617
For you.

772
00:54:14,818 --> 00:54:16,886
- For you.
- What is this?

773
00:54:17,187 --> 00:54:19,189
Working terms and conditions.

774
00:54:20,890 --> 00:54:23,326
Background research for dissertations.

775
00:54:23,693 --> 00:54:24,661
I decline.

776
00:54:25,996 --> 00:54:26,963
Escort to medical conferences.

777
00:54:27,130 --> 00:54:28,131
I decline.

778
00:54:28,331 --> 00:54:29,833
Chauffeur to golf courses.

779
00:54:30,100 --> 00:54:30,934
I decline.

780
00:54:31,067 --> 00:54:32,936
Covering up extramarital affairs.

781
00:54:33,236 --> 00:54:34,304
I decline.

782
00:54:34,504 --> 00:54:36,640
Director's and professors' rounds.

783
00:54:36,840 --> 00:54:37,807
I decline.

784
00:54:37,874 --> 00:54:38,742
I know.

785
00:54:38,808 --> 00:54:40,310
- Brings back memories.
- You remember?

786
00:54:40,377 --> 00:54:41,645
Et cetera, et cetera.

787
00:54:42,445 --> 00:54:45,715
I decline everything that doesn't
require a medical license.

788
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:55,225
Dr. Daimon, as fearless as ever.

789
00:54:55,692 --> 00:54:58,094
With your "I decline" series.

790
00:54:58,862 --> 00:55:00,697
But you work here now.

791
00:55:00,897 --> 00:55:03,500
Won't you sing with us?

792
00:55:03,600 --> 00:55:04,668
Akira.

793
00:55:05,335 --> 00:55:06,670
Add one more condition.

794
00:55:07,037 --> 00:55:07,971
Sure.

795
00:55:08,438 --> 00:55:10,240
Singing "The One and Only"...

796
00:55:11,608 --> 00:55:12,676
I decline.

797
00:55:12,876 --> 00:55:14,110
- I see.
- That's it.

798
00:55:14,978 --> 00:55:18,481
Thank you for your time.

799
00:55:33,496 --> 00:55:37,467
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

800
00:55:48,278 --> 00:55:49,179
Please.

801
00:55:49,379 --> 00:55:50,347
Thanks.

802
00:55:58,655 --> 00:56:00,190
In 2017

803
00:56:00,523 --> 00:56:05,895
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

804
00:56:06,429 --> 00:56:12,502
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

805
00:56:14,070 --> 00:56:14,904
Closer.

806
00:56:17,974 --> 00:56:21,344
Crush Michiko Daimon.

807
00:56:22,946 --> 00:56:27,016
Where's your "yes sir"?
Deputy Chief Surgeon Takashi Torii.

808
00:56:28,351 --> 00:56:31,521
- Yes sir.
- Deputy Chief Surgeon Takashi Ebina?

809
00:56:32,856 --> 00:56:33,723
Yes sir.

810
00:56:33,790 --> 00:56:38,161
Deputy Chief Surgeon Takashi Inomata?

811
00:56:39,262 --> 00:56:42,766
- Yes sir!
- My three loyal Takashis.

812
00:56:43,500 --> 00:56:44,434
Wonderful.

813
00:56:44,901 --> 00:56:47,237
Go, Takashi.

814
00:56:47,837 --> 00:56:50,006
Go, go, Takashi.

815
00:56:50,807 --> 00:56:52,609
Go, fight, win.

816
00:56:53,743 --> 00:56:55,078
Let me introduce her.

817
00:56:55,745 --> 00:56:59,516
My first secretary, Miss Nakatani.

818
00:56:59,682 --> 00:57:02,485
I'm Keiko Nakatani. Nice to meet you.

819
00:57:02,919 --> 00:57:05,321
Keiko, come here.

820
00:57:08,158 --> 00:57:09,692
You're all gawking.

821
00:57:10,527 --> 00:57:11,961
Keep your hands to yourselves.

822
00:57:12,295 --> 00:57:13,296
Yes sir.

823
00:57:13,396 --> 00:57:15,932
He's my second secretary.

824
00:57:16,466 --> 00:57:17,567
I'm Sonta.

825
00:57:17,634 --> 00:57:18,668
Sonta?

826
00:57:19,068 --> 00:57:21,104
Please read between the lines.

827
00:57:21,638 --> 00:57:22,505
Yes sir.

828
00:57:22,605 --> 00:57:24,040
Louder, please.

829
00:57:24,307 --> 00:57:25,241
Yes sir.

830
00:57:26,009 --> 00:57:26,943
Congratulations.

831
00:57:27,010 --> 00:57:28,711
Thank you.

832
00:57:29,179 --> 00:57:30,880
I owe it to you.

833
00:57:38,221 --> 00:57:41,257
Did you hire Michiko Daimon?

834
00:57:41,357 --> 00:57:44,227
Yes. Just as you wished.

835
00:57:46,729 --> 00:57:48,331
Doctor-X.

836
00:57:49,332 --> 00:57:52,268
Surgeries with low success
and survival rates.

837
00:57:52,936 --> 00:57:56,005
Dangerous surgeries with
unestablished procedures.

838
00:57:56,406 --> 00:57:59,309
She'll face their challenges
for a big reward.

839
00:58:01,811 --> 00:58:03,513
Cancer to the medical community.

840
00:58:05,582 --> 00:58:10,653
The type we consider to be
the biggest nuisance.

841
00:58:15,358 --> 00:58:18,895
I understand very well.

842
00:58:19,829 --> 00:58:21,564
Get rid of her.

843
00:58:22,765 --> 00:58:23,900
Yes sir.

844
00:58:28,738 --> 00:58:33,076
<i>In the midst of all this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

845
00:58:33,676 --> 00:58:37,514
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

846
00:58:40,116 --> 00:58:42,151
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

847
00:58:42,785 --> 00:58:46,923
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

848
00:58:47,590 --> 00:58:52,462
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

849
00:58:53,630 --> 00:58:55,899
There she is.

850
00:58:56,799 --> 00:58:58,201
- Daimon!
- Hey!

851
00:59:00,470 --> 00:59:02,839
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

852
00:59:03,339 --> 00:59:06,576
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

853
00:59:06,643 --> 00:59:09,012
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

854
00:59:09,546 --> 00:59:11,447
I never fail.

855
00:59:11,514 --> 00:59:12,549
He's not doing rounds.

856
00:59:12,682 --> 00:59:13,883
I decline.

857
00:59:14,017 --> 00:59:16,319
Thank you for everything.

858
00:59:16,386 --> 00:59:17,420
You'll die without surgery.

859
00:59:17,487 --> 00:59:19,155
I'm not going to have surgery.

860
00:59:19,222 --> 00:59:21,791
- I'd like Dr. Daimon to assist me.
- I decline.

861
00:59:22,759 --> 00:59:23,993
Are you mentally prepared?
